course: dictionary
lesson: 1452
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word case is a good example. «Pack your pens in your pencil case before school.» Here a case is a box that keeps things safe, so you read the words around it to find the right meaning.
explain: «In case of fire, use the stairs, not the lift.» Here case is not a box at all. The words in case of start an instruction for something that might happen. Ask yourself: does the box meaning fit here? If it does not, try another meaning.
explain: «The police will look into the case of the stolen bike.» Here a case is a crime or problem that people investigate. When you meet a word with several meanings, test each one in the sentence and keep the one that makes sense.
fact: Case is a noun: a case, cases.
fact: A case can be a container, such as a suitcase or a phone case.
fact: A case can be one example of something, such as «a case of chickenpox».
fact: «In case» means as a plan for something that might happen, as in «take a coat in case it rains».
fact: In writing, upper case means capital letters and lower case means small letters.
exercise: «Mia put her pens in her pencil case.» What is a pencil case? | *A box for keeping pens and pencils | A type of pencil | A school bag with wheels | A long ruler
exercise: «In case of fire, use the stairs, not the lift.» What does in case of mean here? | Instead of the stairs | Because a fire has already ended | Inside a box of fire | *If this happens, be ready and follow these steps
exercise: In writing, what is upper case? | Small letters | Letters written in pencil | Numbers | *Capital letters
test: «The police will look into the case of the stolen bike.» In this sentence, what is a case? | A box for keeping a bike | A kind of bike | A plan for rain | *A crime or problem that people look into
test: «Take a coat just in case it rains.» Why take a coat? | *As a plan, in case it rains | To carry your lunch in | Because it is cold and wet right now | Because it is your birthday
exam: «The doctor saw a case of chickenpox at school today.» What does case mean here? | A kind of school | *One example of an illness | A box for medicine | A crime at school
